  "Id": 743,
  "Title": "42 patients under treatment at Aga Khan University Hospital for viral haemorrhagic fever",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "At Aga Khan University Hospital (AKUH), 42 patients are currently hospitalized with suspect viral haemorrhagic fever; most of them were admitted during the last two weeks.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClass44BCB987AB38436DA6D895523A17AE1C\"><div>At Aga Khan University Hospital (AKUH), 42 patients are currently hospitalized with suspect viral haemorrhagic fever; most of them were admitted during the last two weeks. This obviously reflects a sudden increase in the number of such cases and is a cause of concern. So far, a total of 159 patients with ages ranging between 6 to 82 years were admitted at AKUH between June 14 to October 16, 2006 with viral haemorrhagic fever. Out of these, six patients expired due to severity of disease, while 111 recovered and were discharged. The patients suffered from symptoms ranging from bleeding, diarrhoea, vomiting to abdominal pain.</div><div><br></div><div>Dr Farhat Abbas, Medical Director and Associate Dean, Clinical Affairs.</div><p><br></p></div>",
